  "Local operation": "Local operation",
  "With \"Email + 2FA Code\" Roborock sends a six digit code by email. There is no input field for it here: enter the code into the state roborock.<instance>.loginCode within 15 minutes of starting the adapter.": "With \"Email + 2FA Code\" Roborock sends a six digit code by email. There is no input field for it here: enter the code into the state roborock.<instance>.loginCode within 15 minutes of starting the adapter.",
  "Connection mode": "Connection mode",
  "Cloud and local": "Cloud and local",
  "Local only (no cloud contact)": "Local only (no cloud contact)",
  "Local only: the adapter never contacts the Roborock cloud. This requires manually configured devices with duid and localKey. Cloud based functions stay unavailable in this mode - map retrieval currently needs the cloud connection, as do saved scenes, firmware information and camera streaming. There is no automatic fallback to the cloud.": "Local only: the adapter never contacts the Roborock cloud. This requires manually configured devices with duid and localKey. Cloud based functions stay unavailable in this mode - map retrieval currently needs the cloud connection, as do saved scenes, firmware information and camera streaming. There is no automatic fallback to the cloud.",
  "Manual devices (JSON)": "Manual devices (JSON)",
  "JSON array, one object per device: {\"duid\": \"...\", \"localKey\": \"...\", \"ip\": \"192.168.1.50\", \"pv\": \"1.0\"}. Optional: name, model, category, sn. The localKey is a 16 character device secret that only exists in the Roborock cloud device list and cannot be derived locally; it changes only when the device is paired again. Log in once with your account to read it, then keep it here. It is stored encrypted and never written to the log.": "JSON array, one object per device: {\"duid\": \"...\", \"localKey\": \"...\", \"ip\": \"192.168.1.50\", \"pv\": \"1.0\"}. Optional: name, model, category, sn. The localKey is a 16 character device secret that only exists in the Roborock cloud device list and cannot be derived locally; it changes only when the device is paired again. Log in once with your account to read it, then keep it here. It is stored encrypted and never written to the log.",
  "Search devices in network": "Search devices in network",
  "Listens for device broadcasts and reports duid, IP address and protocol version, so a manual entry can be created without a cloud account. The adapter instance must be running.": "Listens for device broadcasts and reports duid, IP address and protocol version, so a manual entry can be created without a cloud account. The adapter instance must be running.",
  "Listen for device broadcasts (UDP 58866)": "Listen for device broadcasts (UDP 58866)",
  "Off: only devices with a statically configured IP address are used. Helpful when broadcasts are filtered (VLAN, WLAN client isolation, LXC or Docker bridges).": "Off: only devices with a statically configured IP address are used. Helpful when broadcasts are filtered (VLAN, WLAN client isolation, LXC or Docker bridges).",
  "Network interface for discovery": "Network interface for discovery",
  "IP address of the interface the UDP discovery socket binds to. Empty means all interfaces, which can fail on hosts with several networks.": "IP address of the interface the UDP discovery socket binds to. Empty means all interfaces, which can fail on hosts with several networks.",
  "JSON array of { duid, localKey, ip, pv }. The localKey is a device secret and is stored encrypted.": "JSON array of { duid, localKey, ip, pv }. The localKey is a device secret and is stored encrypted.",
